Statements:
[
    "Retriever failures are grouped into three categories: coverage/completeness, relevancy, and ranking/order.",
    "Coverage/completeness is defined as how much of the total relevant context the retriever can fetch.",
    "The metric for coverage/completeness is contextual recall.",
    "Tunable parameters for coverage/completeness include chunking hyperparameters, topk, and the embedding model or embedding stage.",
    "If recall is low, increase chunk size and/or increase topk.",
    "Relevancy is defined as how relevant the retrieved results are to the query.",
    "The metric for relevancy is contextual relevancy.",
    "Tunable parameters for relevancy include chunking hyperparameters, the embedding model, and topk.",
    "If relevancy is low, decrease chunk size.",
    "Ranking/order is defined as how well the retriever orders results by relevance.",
    "The metric for ranking/order is precision.",
    "Tunable parameters for ranking/order include a reranker, the embedding model, topk, and chunking choices.",
    "A cross-encoder reranker can recalculate similarities and improve ranking.",
    "Chunking and the embedding stage are the main places to tune because they affect the retriever.",
    "Metrics are applied together across the application but target different components.",
    "You can tweak the specific component indicated by the metric."
] 

